#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Map operator representations for the latest version of Qiskit bosons"
msgstr "Petakan perwakilan pengendali untuk versi terkini Qiskit bosons"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Map operator representations"
msgstr "Petakan perwakilan pengendali"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"mappers-explanation\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Map operator representations {#map-operator-representations}"
msgstr "Petakan perwakilan pengendali {#map-operator-representations}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A **mapper** turns a [`BosonOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator\") into a qubit operator, here a [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable). The operator itself knows nothing about qubits: it stores ladder operators on modes, and a bosonic mode holds arbitrarily many particles. Everything that makes the operator finite (how many occupation levels you keep, and how those levels are laid out on qubits) is decided when you map it.\n"
msgstr "Sebuah **pemeta** menukarkan [`BosonOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator\") menjadi pengendali qubit, di sini [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable). Pengendali itu sendiri tidak tahu apa-apa tentang qubit: ia menyimpan pengendali tangga pada mod, dan sesuatu mod boson memuatkan zarah dalam bilangan sembarangan. Segala yang menjadikan pengendali itu terhingga (berapa banyak aras penghunian yang anda simpan, dan bagaimana aras itu disusun pada qubit) ditentukan semasa anda memetakannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The library mapper [`occupation_encoding()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-library-occupation-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.library.occupation_encoding \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.library.occupation_encoding\") works in the occupation (Fock) basis: level $n$ of a mode is the state with $n$ bosons. It takes the operator and a [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\"), which holds the truncation and the encoding. This guide explains what those two choices mean and what each one costs. For an end-to-end route that uses them, see [Simulate Bose-Hubbard dynamics with a choice of encoding](bose-hubbard#bose-hubbard-getting-started); for how the transpiler applies the same choices to a whole circuit, see [Transpile bosonic circuits](transpilation#transpilation-explanation).\n"
msgstr "Pemeta pustaka [`occupation_encoding()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-library-occupation-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.library.occupation_encoding \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.library.occupation_encoding\") bekerja dalam asas penghunian (Fock): aras $n$ bagi sesuatu mod ialah keadaan dengan $n$ boson. Ia menerima pengendali dan sebuah [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\"), yang menyimpan pemangkasan dan pengekodan. Panduan ini menerangkan maksud kedua-dua pilihan itu dan kos setiap satu. Untuk laluan hujung ke hujung yang menggunakannya, lihat [Simulasikan dinamik Bose-Hubbard dengan pilihan pengekodan](bose-hubbard#bose-hubbard-getting-started); untuk cara Transpiler menerapkan pilihan yang sama pada keseluruhan litar, lihat [Transpile litar boson](transpilation#transpilation-explanation).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"truncation-explanation\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Truncate the Fock space {#truncate-the-fock-space}"
msgstr "Pangkas ruang Fock {#truncate-the-fock-space}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A mode that is kept to $d = n_\\text{max} + 1$ levels, where $n_\\text{max}$ is its `max_occupation`, no longer obeys the canonical commutation relation. Writing $\\bar{b}$ for the annihilation operator truncated to those levels,\n"
msgstr "Sesuatu mod yang dikekalkan pada $d = n_\\text{max} + 1$ aras, dengan $n_\\text{max}$ ialah `max_occupation`nya, tidak lagi mematuhi hubungan kalis tukar kanonik. Menulis $\\bar{b}$ bagi pengendali pemusnah yang dipangkas kepada aras-aras tersebut,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"[\\bar{b}, \\bar{b}^\\dagger] = 1 - d \\, \\lvert d-1 \\rangle\\langle d-1 \\rvert \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"[\\bar{b}, \\bar{b}^\\dagger] = 1 - d \\, \\lvert d-1 \\rangle\\langle d-1 \\rvert \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "so the relation holds on every level except the highest <span id=\"id1\" />[\\[1\\]](#id4). You can see this by mapping the commutator of the two ladder operators and reading its diagonal on the levels of one mode. The following helper builds the dense matrix of a mapped operator for a single mode, which is only reasonable for very small registers:\n"
msgstr "maka hubungan itu berlaku pada setiap aras kecuali yang tertinggi <span id=\"id1\" />[\\[1\\]](#id4). Anda boleh melihat ini dengan memetakan komutator kedua-dua pengendali tangga dan membaca pepenjurunya pada aras satu mod. Pembantu berikut membina matriks tumpat bagi pengendali yang dipetakan untuk satu mod, yang hanya munasabah untuk daftar yang sangat kecil:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The last entry is $1 - d$. Because this means the span of $\\{\\bar{b}^\\dagger, \\bar{b}\\}$ is not closed under the commutator, no encoding is an isomorphism of algebras. An encoding maps *states*, together with the operators that act within the truncated subspace. The following two consequences matter in practice.\n"
msgstr "Entri terakhir ialah $1 - d$. Oleh sebab ini bermakna rentang $\\{\\bar{b}^\\dagger, \\bar{b}\\}$ tidak tertutup di bawah komutator, tiada pengekodan yang merupakan isomorfisme aljabar. Sesuatu pengekodan memetakan *keadaan*, bersama pengendali yang bertindak dalam subruang terpangkas. Dua akibat berikut penting dalam amalan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The cutoff must bound the reachable occupation.** It is not enough to bound the occupation you start with. A beamsplitter acting on $\\lvert 1, 1 \\rangle$ populates $\\lvert 2, 0 \\rangle$ and $\\lvert 0, 2 \\rangle$, so a cutoff of one silently produces a wrong state:\n"
msgstr "**Hadnya mesti mengikat penghunian yang boleh dicapai.** Tidak cukup untuk mengikat penghunian yang anda mulakan. Pemecah alur yang bertindak pada $\\lvert 1, 1 \\rangle$ mengisi $\\lvert 2, 0 \\rangle$ dan $\\lvert 0, 2 \\rangle$, jadi had satu secara senyap menghasilkan keadaan yang salah:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With a cutoff of one, the probability of staying in $\\lvert 1, 1 \\rangle$ is one, because the two states that the dynamics would populate do not exist. With a cutoff of two, it vanishes, which is the Hong-Ou-Mandel effect. This is why `max_occupation` is a required argument that never has a default: it is a modeling decision and a convergence parameter that you are expected to sweep.\n"
msgstr "Dengan had satu, kebarangkalian kekal dalam $\\lvert 1, 1 \\rangle$ ialah satu, kerana kedua-dua keadaan yang akan diisi oleh dinamik itu tidak wujud. Dengan had dua, ia lenyap, iaitu kesan Hong-Ou-Mandel. Inilah sebabnya `max_occupation` ialah hujah wajib yang tidak pernah mempunyai nilai lalai: ia ialah keputusan pemodelan dan parameter penumpuan yang anda dijangka sapu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Mapping does not commute with normal ordering.** The operators $b b^\\dagger$ and $b^\\dagger b + 1$ are equal before truncation, but they map to different qubit operators:\n"
msgstr "**Pemetaan tidak berkomutasi dengan penyusunan normal.** Pengendali $b b^\\dagger$ dan $b^\\dagger b + 1$ adalah sama sebelum pemangkasan, tetapi keduanya dipetakan kepada pengendali qubit yang berbeza:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two agree on every level but the highest. Applied to the top level, $b^\\dagger$ has nowhere to go and the amplitude is clipped, so $b b^\\dagger$ is zero there, whereas $b^\\dagger b + 1$ gives $d$. Decide once whether your Hamiltonian is defined in normal-ordered form, and map that form consistently.\n"
msgstr "Kedua-duanya sepadan pada setiap aras kecuali yang tertinggi. Apabila dikenakan pada aras teratas, $b^\\dagger$ tiada tempat untuk dituju dan amplitud dipotong, jadi $b b^\\dagger$ ialah sifar di situ, manakala $b^\\dagger b + 1$ memberikan $d$. Tentukan sekali sama ada Hamiltonian anda ditakrifkan dalam bentuk tersusun normal, dan petakan bentuk itu secara konsisten.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Three methods help you choose a cutoff, and all of them are lower bounds. The operator reports the largest number of creation operators that it applies to each mode within a single term, and a spec compares that with its cutoffs:\n"
msgstr "Tiga kaedah membantu anda memilih had, dan kesemuanya ialah batas bawah. Pengendali melaporkan bilangan terbesar pengendali penciptaan yang dikenakannya pada setiap mod dalam satu sebutan, dan sesuatu spesifikasi membandingkannya dengan hadnya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A non-zero entry means the cutoff is below the bound, and the value is how far. These helpers do not know about the dynamics, so a passing check does not make a cutoff sufficient; the beamsplitter above has a bound of one yet needs a cutoff of two. They can also report a shortfall for a term that is zero on the retained levels, as $b^\\dagger b^\\dagger b b$ is for a cutoff of one.\n"
msgstr "Entri bukan sifar bermakna had berada di bawah batas, dan nilainya ialah seberapa jauh. Pembantu ini tidak mengetahui tentang dinamik, jadi semakan yang lulus tidak menjadikan sesuatu had mencukupi; pemecah alur di atas mempunyai batas satu tetapi memerlukan had dua. Ia juga boleh melaporkan kekurangan bagi sebutan yang bernilai sifar pada aras yang dikekalkan, seperti $b^\\dagger b^\\dagger b b$ bagi had satu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"level-spec-explanation\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Describe the truncation with a LevelSpec {#describe-the-truncation-with-a-levelspec}"
msgstr "Huraikan pemangkasan dengan LevelSpec {#describe-the-truncation-with-a-levelspec}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\") bundles the cutoff of every mode with the encoding, and it derives from them how many qubits each mode occupies and where its qubits start. Everything that has to agree about that (the mapper, the transpiler layout, the state preparation) is given the same spec. The encoding is a required argument, and so is the cutoff: neither has a default.\n"
msgstr "Sebuah [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\") menghimpunkan had setiap mod bersama pengekodan, dan daripadanya ia memperoleh berapa banyak qubit yang diduduki setiap mod serta di mana qubitnya bermula. Segala yang perlu bersetuju tentang itu (pemeta, susun atur Transpiler, penyediaan keadaan) diberikan spesifikasi yang sama. Pengekodan ialah hujah wajib, begitu juga had: kedua-duanya tidak mempunyai nilai lalai.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The cutoff is either one integer, shared by all modes, or one integer per mode:\n"
msgstr "Had ialah sama ada satu integer yang dikongsi oleh semua mod, atau satu integer bagi setiap mod:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A spec built from a single integer leaves the number of modes open, so you have to resolve it before asking for widths. A sequence is never broadcast, whatever its length, and it fixes the number of modes:\n"
msgstr "Spesifikasi yang dibina daripada satu integer membiarkan bilangan mod terbuka, jadi anda perlu menyelesaikannya sebelum meminta lebar. Satu jujukan tidak pernah disiarkan, walau apa pun panjangnya, dan ia menetapkan bilangan mod:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mode $m$ occupies the qubits `offsets[m]` to `offsets[m] + widths[m] - 1`, so modes with different cutoffs can take different numbers of qubits, and the offsets are the running sum of the widths. You do not need to pass the number of modes to the mapper. It takes it from the spec, or, for a spec with a single cutoff, from the operator through [`min_num_modes()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes\"). The register can be wider than the modes need; the surplus qubits are idle and sit at the end:\n"
msgstr "Mod $m$ menduduki qubit `offsets[m]` hingga `offsets[m] + widths[m] - 1`, jadi mod dengan had berbeza boleh mengambil bilangan qubit yang berbeza, dan ofset ialah hasil tambah berjalan bagi lebar. Anda tidak perlu menghantar bilangan mod kepada pemeta. Ia mengambilnya daripada spesifikasi, atau, bagi spesifikasi dengan satu had, daripada pengendali melalui [`min_num_modes()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes\"). Daftar boleh lebih lebar daripada keperluan mod; qubit lebihan tidak aktif dan terletak di hujung:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An operator that acts on a mode beyond the last one of a per-mode spec is refused:\n"
msgstr "Pengendali yang bertindak pada mod di luar mod terakhir bagi spesifikasi per-mod akan ditolak:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A few limits follow from how the encodings count qubits. Under a compact encoding, a mode with a single level (`max_occupation = 0`) takes no qubit at all, because its one level needs nothing to be told apart from another. Such a mode is allowed and does not move the qubits of the modes after it, but a spec in which every mode would take no qubit is rejected. The unary encodings hold at most 128 levels per mode, and a larger cutoff raises an error that suggests a compact encoding:\n"
msgstr "Beberapa had timbul daripada cara pengekodan mengira qubit. Di bawah pengekodan padat, mod dengan satu aras sahaja (`max_occupation = 0`) tidak mengambil qubit langsung, kerana satu-satunya arasnya tidak memerlukan apa-apa untuk dibezakan daripada yang lain. Mod sebegini dibenarkan dan tidak menggerakkan qubit mod selepasnya, tetapi spesifikasi yang setiap modnya tidak mengambil qubit akan ditolak. Pengekodan unari memuatkan paling banyak 128 aras bagi setiap mod, dan had yang lebih besar menimbulkan ralat yang mencadangkan pengekodan padat:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose an encoding {#choose-an-encoding}"
msgstr "Pilih pengekodan {#choose-an-encoding}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A [`LevelEncoding`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding\") decides which basis state of a block of qubits represents each level. There are four, and no one of them is best in general <span id=\"id2\" />[\\[2\\]](#id5). The number of qubits per mode and the bit pattern of each level follow from the encoding:\n"
msgstr "Sebuah [`LevelEncoding`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding\") menentukan keadaan asas bagi blok qubit yang mewakili setiap aras. Terdapat empat, dan tiada satu pun yang terbaik secara umum <span id=\"id2\" />[\\[2\\]](#id5). Bilangan qubit bagi setiap mod dan corak bit bagi setiap aras mengikut pengekodan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The bit patterns are integers in which bit $q$ is the value of qubit $q$. The unary encodings spend one qubit per level and set one of them. The compact encodings spend $\\lceil \\log_2 d \\rceil$ qubits and store the level number, in binary or as a Gray code in which neighboring levels differ in one bit. The string name of an encoding is accepted wherever the encoding is.\n"
msgstr "Corak bit ialah integer yang bit $q$ merupakan nilai qubit $q$. Pengekodan unari menggunakan satu qubit bagi setiap aras dan menetapkan satu daripadanya. Pengekodan padat menggunakan $\\lceil \\log_2 d \\rceil$ qubit dan menyimpan nombor aras, dalam binari atau sebagai kod Gray yang aras berjirannya berbeza dalam satu bit. Nama rentetan bagi sesuatu pengekodan diterima di mana-mana pengekodan diterima.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The trade-off is qubits against operator weight. The compact encodings need exponentially fewer qubits, but a ladder operator connects levels whose patterns can differ in several bits, so its terms act on more qubits. The following sections look at what this costs, starting with the two unary encodings, which have identical layouts and differ only in the operator.\n"
msgstr "Pertukaran ganti ialah qubit berbanding berat pengendali. Pengekodan padat memerlukan qubit yang jauh lebih sedikit secara eksponen, tetapi pengendali tangga menghubungkan aras yang coraknya boleh berbeza dalam beberapa bit, jadi sebutannya bertindak pada lebih banyak qubit. Bahagian berikut meneliti kosnya, bermula dengan dua pengekodan unari, yang mempunyai susun atur yang sama dan hanya berbeza pada pengendali.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"unary-variants-explanation\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compare the two unary encodings {#compare-the-two-unary-encodings}"
msgstr "Bandingkan dua pengekodan unari {#compare-the-two-unary-encodings}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the unary encoding a ladder operator moves one excitation between two neighboring qubits. To write that as an operator on the whole mode, you must choose what to do with the other qubits. The two variants choose differently:\n"
msgstr "Dalam pengekodan unari, pengendali tangga menggerakkan satu pengujaan antara dua qubit berjiran. Untuk menulisnya sebagai pengendali pada seluruh mod, anda mesti memilih apa yang dilakukan pada qubit lain. Kedua-dua varian memilih secara berbeza:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`unary_projected` puts a projector $\\lvert 0 \\rangle\\langle 0 \\rvert$ on every other qubit of the mode. That enforces the one-hot constraint in the operator itself: the term acts only if the rest of the mode is empty.\n"
msgstr "`unary_projected` meletakkan unjuran $\\lvert 0 \\rangle\\langle 0 \\rvert$ pada setiap qubit lain dalam mod itu. Itu menguatkuasakan kekangan satu-panas dalam pengendali itu sendiri: sebutan hanya bertindak jika bakinya mod itu kosong.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`unary_unprojected` leaves those qubits alone, so the term acts as the identity on them.\n"
msgstr "`unary_unprojected` membiarkan qubit tersebut, jadi sebutan bertindak sebagai identiti padanya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Look at a single $b^\\dagger$ at $d = 4$ under both. The mapper returns a [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable), whose terms are strings of single-qubit bit terms. Here are the first four terms of each, with the qubits they act on:\n"
msgstr "Lihat satu $b^\\dagger$ pada $d = 4$ di bawah kedua-duanya. Pemeta mengembalikan [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable), yang sebutannya ialah rentetan sebutan bit qubit tunggal. Berikut ialah empat sebutan pertama setiap satu, dengan qubit yang dikenakan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both have twelve terms with the same coefficients. The projected terms carry a `0` bit term on the two qubits that the unprojected terms do not mention, so each projected term touches all four qubits and each unprojected term touches two. In general a projected term touches all $d$ qubits of the mode, because it carries two factors, each $X$ or $Y$, and a projector on each other qubit.\n"
msgstr "Kedua-duanya mempunyai dua belas sebutan dengan pekali yang sama. Sebutan terunjur membawa sebutan bit `0` pada dua qubit yang tidak disebut oleh sebutan tak terunjur, jadi setiap sebutan terunjur menyentuh keempat-empat qubit dan setiap sebutan tak terunjur menyentuh dua. Secara umum sebutan terunjur menyentuh semua $d$ qubit bagi mod itu, kerana ia membawa dua faktor, masing-masing $X$ atau $Y$, dan satu unjuran pada setiap qubit lain.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two operators are equal on the states that the encoding is meant for, the one-hot basis states (the codewords), and differ outside them. To check, take a small operator on two modes at $d = 3$ and compare the matrices on the nine codewords:\n"
msgstr "Kedua-dua pengendali adalah sama pada keadaan yang dimaksudkan oleh pengekodan, iaitu keadaan asas satu-panas (kata kod), dan berbeza di luarnya. Untuk menyemak, ambil pengendali kecil pada dua mod pada $d = 3$ dan bandingkan matriks pada sembilan kata kod:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both also leave the codeword subspace invariant, so a state prepared on a codeword stays on codewords. The choice matters only for states that leave that subspace, for example through noise. There the projected operator suppresses the evolution, because its projectors fail, whereas the unprojected one keeps acting. Neither behavior is a physical requirement. The unprojected operator is only defined on the one-hot subspace, so choosing it is a modeling decision and not a free optimization.\n"
msgstr "Kedua-duanya juga membiarkan subruang kata kod tidak berubah, jadi keadaan yang disediakan pada kata kod kekal pada kata kod. Pilihan ini penting hanya untuk keadaan yang meninggalkan subruang itu, contohnya melalui hingar. Di situ pengendali terunjur menekan evolusi, kerana unjurannya gagal, manakala yang tak terunjur terus bertindak. Tiada satu pun kelakuan itu merupakan keperluan fizikal. Pengendali tak terunjur hanya ditakrifkan pada subruang satu-panas, jadi memilihnya ialah keputusan pemodelan dan bukan pengoptimuman percuma.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "What the projectors cost is gates. Evolve a Hermitian $b^\\dagger + b$ on one mode for a short time, and count the two-qubit gates after Qiskit’s transpilation:\n"
msgstr "Kos unjuran ialah Gate. Evolusikan $b^\\dagger + b$ yang Hermitian pada satu mod untuk masa yang singkat, dan kira Gate dua-qubit selepas transpilasi Qiskit:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The exact counts depend on how Qiskit synthesizes the evolution gate, which changes between releases, so plot them:\n"
msgstr "Kiraan tepat bergantung pada cara Qiskit mensintesis Gate evolusi, yang berubah antara keluaran, jadi plotkannya:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![CX count against the number of levels d for the four encodings. The unary\\_projected count grows fastest, the unary\\_unprojected count grows linearly, and the Gray code is the cheapest.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/mappers-14.avif)\n"
msgstr "![CX count against the number of levels d for the four encodings. The unary\\_projected count grows fastest, the unary\\_unprojected count grows linearly, and the Gray code is the cheapest.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/mappers-14.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The unprojected count grows linearly with $d$, because each of the $d - 1$ transitions is a two-qubit rotation. The projected count grows much faster, because every term acts on all $d$ qubits. The compact encodings need fewer qubits, but the weight of their terms depends on how the bit patterns of neighboring levels differ: the Gray code, in which they differ in one bit, is the cheaper of the two compact encodings, and standard binary jumps when a carry flips several bits at once ($d = 5$). Whether a compact encoding also beats the unprojected unary one depends on $d$ and on how Qiskit synthesizes the evolution, so read the trend and not the ranking at one size.\n"
msgstr "Kiraan tak terunjur meningkat secara linear dengan $d$, kerana setiap satu daripada $d - 1$ peralihan ialah putaran dua-qubit. Kiraan terunjur meningkat jauh lebih pantas, kerana setiap sebutan bertindak pada semua $d$ qubit. Pengekodan padat memerlukan lebih sedikit qubit, tetapi berat sebutannya bergantung pada bagaimana corak bit aras berjiran berbeza: kod Gray, yang berbeza dalam satu bit, ialah yang lebih murah antara dua pengekodan padat, dan binari piawai melonjak apabila bawa membalikkan beberapa bit serentak ($d = 5$). Sama ada pengekodan padat juga mengatasi unari tak terunjur bergantung pada $d$ dan pada cara Qiskit mensintesis evolusi, jadi bacalah trendnya dan bukan kedudukan pada satu saiz.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The projectors also matter when you expand a mapped operator into Paulis, which [`from_sparse_observable()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp#from_sparse_observable) does by replacing each projector with a sum of two Pauli operators. A term with $k$ projectors becomes $2^k$ Pauli terms. Here is a single $b^\\dagger$ at small $d$, which is the only size at which you should try this:\n"
msgstr "Unjuran juga penting apabila anda mengembangkan pengendali yang dipetakan kepada Pauli, yang dilakukan oleh [`from_sparse_observable()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp#from_sparse_observable) dengan menggantikan setiap unjuran dengan hasil tambah dua pengendali Pauli. Sebutan dengan $k$ unjuran menjadi $2^k$ sebutan Pauli. Berikut ialah satu $b^\\dagger$ pada $d$ kecil, iaitu satu-satunya saiz yang patut anda cuba:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both variants store the same number of terms, but the expansion of the projected one grows exponentially in $d$. For anything larger than a toy example, read the terms of the [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable) directly, as the listing above does, instead of converting it.\n"
msgstr "Kedua-dua varian menyimpan bilangan sebutan yang sama, tetapi pengembangan yang terunjur meningkat secara eksponen dalam $d$. Untuk apa-apa yang lebih besar daripada contoh mainan, baca sebutan [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable) secara terus, seperti senarai di atas, dan jangan menukarnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The compact encodings cannot drop their projectors. There the zero bits are part of the level number, so removing a $\\lvert 0 \\rangle\\langle 0 \\rvert$ changes which levels a term connects, and the operator is no longer the same on the codewords. This is why only the unary encoding comes in two variants.\n"
msgstr "Pengekodan padat tidak boleh menggugurkan unjurannya. Di sana bit sifar merupakan sebahagian daripada nombor aras, jadi membuang $\\lvert 0 \\rangle\\langle 0 \\rvert$ mengubah aras yang dihubungkan oleh sesuatu sebutan, dan pengendali tidak lagi sama pada kata kod. Inilah sebabnya hanya pengekodan unari mempunyai dua varian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "A product of ladders is truncated first {#a-product-of-ladders-is-truncated-first}"
msgstr "Hasil darab tangga dipangkas dahulu {#a-product-of-ladders-is-truncated-first}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "One more design choice shows up in the cost of diagonal terms. The mapper does not map each ladder operator and multiply the results. It collects the ladder operators that a term applies to one mode, multiplies them as a $d \\times d$ matrix in the Fock basis, truncates that product once, and encodes the result <span id=\"id3\" />[\\[2\\]](#id5). A product such as the number operator $b^\\dagger b$ therefore stays diagonal:\n"
msgstr "Satu lagi pilihan reka bentuk muncul dalam kos sebutan pepenjuru. Pemeta tidak memetakan setiap pengendali tangga dan mendarabkan hasilnya. Ia mengumpulkan pengendali tangga yang dikenakan oleh sesuatu sebutan pada satu mod, mendarabkannya sebagai matriks $d \\times d$ dalam asas Fock, memangkas hasil darab itu sekali, dan mengekodkan hasilnya <span id=\"id3\" />[\\[2\\]](#id5). Hasil darab seperti pengendali nombor $b^\\dagger b$ oleh itu kekal pepenjuru:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Its terms are the projectors $\\lvert 1 \\rangle\\langle 1 \\rvert$ on the qubit of each level above zero, weighted by the level number (level zero has weight zero and so has no term). A time evolution of it is a set of single-qubit rotations and needs no two-qubit gate. Multiplying the two mapped ladder operators instead gives the same operator on the codewords, but a different one outside them, with off-diagonal strings that cost gates:\n"
msgstr "Sebutannya ialah unjuran $\\lvert 1 \\rangle\\langle 1 \\rvert$ pada qubit setiap aras di atas sifar, dibebani oleh nombor aras (aras sifar mempunyai berat sifar dan oleh itu tiada sebutan). Evolusi masanya ialah satu set putaran qubit tunggal dan tidak memerlukan Gate dua-qubit. Mendarabkan dua pengendali tangga yang dipetakan sebaliknya memberikan pengendali yang sama pada kata kod, tetapi yang berbeza di luarnya, dengan rentetan luar-pepenjuru yang memerlukan kos Gate:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Diagonal terms such as the on-site interaction of the Bose-Hubbard model are these products, which is where this choice matters.\n"
msgstr "Sebutan pepenjuru seperti interaksi pada-tapak model Bose-Hubbard ialah hasil darab ini, di situlah pilihan ini penting.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Write a custom mapper {#write-a-custom-mapper}"
msgstr "Tulis pemeta tersuai {#write-a-custom-mapper}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you want an encoding that the library does not provide, build it from the image of a single ladder operator. [`map_boson_action_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-map-boson-action-generators#qiskit_bosons.mappers.map_boson_action_generators \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.map_boson_action_generators\") takes a function that maps one [`BosonAction`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-action-boson-action#qiskit_bosons.operators.boson_action.BosonAction \"qiskit_bosons.operators.boson_action.BosonAction\"), a function that returns the identity, and builds the mapper of whole operators from them. It multiplies the images of the actions of each term in order, scales by the coefficient, and sums the terms. The output can be any type that supports scalar multiplication and composition.\n"
msgstr "Jika anda mahukan pengekodan yang tidak disediakan oleh pustaka, bina daripada imej satu pengendali tangga. [`map_boson_action_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-map-boson-action-generators#qiskit_bosons.mappers.map_boson_action_generators \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.map_boson_action_generators\") menerima fungsi yang memetakan satu [`BosonAction`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-action-boson-action#qiskit_bosons.operators.boson_action.BosonAction \"qiskit_bosons.operators.boson_action.BosonAction\"), fungsi yang mengembalikan identiti, dan membina pemeta pengendali keseluruhan daripadanya. Ia mendarabkan imej tindakan setiap sebutan mengikut susunan, menskala dengan pekali, dan menjumlahkan sebutan. Outputnya boleh jenis apa pun yang menyokong pendaraban skalar dan gubahan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As an example, take the encoding for $d = 2$ that stores a mode in one qubit. A creation operator is $\\lvert 1 \\rangle\\langle 0 \\rvert$, which is $(X - iY)/2$ in Qiskit’s convention, and an annihilation operator is its adjoint:\n"
msgstr "Sebagai contoh, ambil pengekodan untuk $d = 2$ yang menyimpan satu mod dalam satu qubit. Pengendali penciptaan ialah $\\lvert 1 \\rangle\\langle 0 \\rvert$, iaitu $(X - iY)/2$ dalam konvensyen Qiskit, dan pengendali pemusnah ialah adjointnya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This hand-written mapper multiplies the mapped ladder operators, and it agrees with the library mapper here because every mode has two levels and a qubit holds the whole mode. At larger $d$, as the previous section showed, composing the mapped ladders and truncating the product first are not the same operator outside the codewords.\n"
msgstr "Pemeta tulisan tangan ini mendarabkan pengendali tangga yang dipetakan, dan ia sepadan dengan pemeta pustaka di sini kerana setiap mod mempunyai dua aras dan satu qubit memuatkan keseluruhan mod. Pada $d$ yang lebih besar, seperti yang ditunjukkan bahagian sebelumnya, menggubah tangga yang dipetakan dan memangkas hasil darab dahulu bukanlah pengendali yang sama di luar kata kod.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To use such a mapper in a circuit, wrap it in a function with the signature `(operator, num_qubits) -> SparseObservable` and hand it to [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\"), which maps the operator of every [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate with it. The transpiler pipeline is described in [Transpile bosonic circuits](transpilation#transpilation-explanation).\n"
msgstr "Untuk menggunakan pemeta sebegini dalam litar, bungkus dalam fungsi dengan tandatangan `(operator, num_qubits) -> SparseObservable` dan serahkan kepada [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\"), yang memetakan pengendali setiap Gate [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") dengannya. Saluran paip Transpiler diterangkan dalam [Transpile litar boson](transpilation#transpilation-explanation).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two details are worth knowing. First, the qubit operator must have real coefficients, because [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate) rejects an imaginary part. A Hermitian operator maps to a real one, but only once the terms that cancel have been merged. This hand-written mapper does not merge them, so a hopping term and its adjoint leave imaginary coefficients behind until you simplify the result. The library mapper merges its own result; a custom one has to do it, for example by wrapping it in [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-synthesis-simplify#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.simplify\"):\n"
msgstr "Dua butiran wajar diketahui. Pertama, pengendali qubit mesti mempunyai pekali nyata, kerana [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate) menolak bahagian khayal. Pengendali Hermitian dipetakan kepada yang nyata, tetapi hanya selepas sebutan yang saling membatalkan digabungkan. Pemeta tulisan tangan ini tidak menggabungkannya, jadi sebutan lompatan dan adjointnya meninggalkan pekali khayal sehingga anda memudahkan hasilnya. Pemeta pustaka menggabungkan hasilnya sendiri; pemeta tersuai perlu melakukannya, contohnya dengan membungkusnya dalam [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-synthesis-simplify#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.simplify\"):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Second, a product formula synthesizes the terms in the order it receives them, and the order a mapper produces is not guaranteed to be stable. The helpers [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-synthesis-simplify#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.simplify\") and [`group_wise()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-synthesis-group-wise#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.group_wise \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.group_wise\") wrap a mapper function to control it: `simplify` merges duplicate strings and sorts the terms into a canonical order, whereas `group_wise` maps one group of the operator at a time so that the terms of a group stay adjacent. Do not combine the two, because sorting discards the grouping. The [grouping guide](grouping#grouping-explanation) shows how to assign groups, and the [synthesis guide](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-explanation) shows how the order affects the circuit.\n"
msgstr "Kedua, formula hasil darab mensintesis sebutan mengikut susunan ia menerimanya, dan susunan yang dihasilkan pemeta tidak dijamin stabil. Pembantu [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-synthesis-simplify#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.simplify\") dan [`group_wise()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-synthesis-group-wise#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.group_wise \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.group_wise\") membungkus fungsi pemeta untuk mengawalnya: `simplify` menggabungkan rentetan pendua dan mengisih sebutan ke dalam susunan kanonik, manakala `group_wise` memetakan satu kumpulan pengendali pada satu masa supaya sebutan sesuatu kumpulan kekal bersebelahan. Jangan gabungkan kedua-duanya, kerana pengisihan membuang pengumpulan. [Panduan pengumpulan](grouping#grouping-explanation) menunjukkan cara menetapkan kumpulan, dan [panduan sintesis](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-explanation) menunjukkan bagaimana susunan menjejaskan litar.\n"

